id: pm-x0iv17
title: "The one projection that promises completeness is the one that loses data: pm contracts --full drops all 76 structured command summaries, returns 160 bare name strings, and reports has_omissions false"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,contracts,omission-receipt,projection,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:17:35.056Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T18:18:10.921Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Either --full is a strict superset of the default projection, or its omission receipt names every field group it drops with an accurate restore hint; One key name carries one row shape across every projection of a command; a key does not mean structured records in one projection and bare strings in another; A gate proves, for every command that declares projections, that a projection reporting has_omissions false is field-wise complete against every narrower projection of the same command; The agent-facing cold start keeps working from the declared row_contract without the agent having to discover which projection happens to carry the intent metadata"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "A projection that declares has_omissions false carries everything the narrower projections carry, so an agent that follows the receipt's own restore_with hint never loses a field it already had."
actual_result: "pm contracts --json returns command_summaries with 76 structured records (command, intent, flags, default_max_estimated_tokens) and an empty commands array, and declares has_omissions true with restore_with --full. Following that hint, pm contracts --full --json returns command_summaries empty and commands as 160 bare strings including subcommand spellings like 'beads import' — the intent, flag and token-budget metadata is gone — while declaring has_omissions false."
